  "notes": [
    "**Haber** is completely irregular in all tenses",
    "Primary use: auxiliary verb for perfect tenses (*he comido* - I have eaten)",
    "Past participle: **habido** (rarely used except in perfect tenses of haber itself)",
    "Future: irregular stem \"habr-\" (not \"haber-\")",
    "Condicional: irregular stem \"habr-\" + conditional endings",
    "Impersonal forms for \"there is/are\":",
    "Present: **hay** (there is/are)",
    "Preterite: **hubo** (there was/were)",
    "Imperfect: **había** (there was/were)",
    "Perfect: **ha habido** (there has/have been)",
    "Future: **habrá** (there will be)",
    "Conditional: **habría** (there would be)",
    "The preterite forms (hube, hubiste, etc.) are rarely used in everyday speech",
    "Don't confuse with **tener** (to have/possess)"
  ],
